s situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities) but concerns (unfriendly, eats unhealthily, unorganized, not good at taking criticism). We can bring that up to compare.\n\nThus as Agent 3, we can say: \"I still support Candidate C, but I want to highlight that Candidate A, while technically strong, has significant reliability and crew cooperation concerns (unfriendly, unorganized, poor criticism handling) that make him less suitable. Candidate D, despite strong problem solving and responsibility, has moody and loner traits that could impair crew cooperation. Candidate B's uncooperative behavior also disqualifies him. Therefore, Candidate C remains the best.\" That would be a contribution.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: we agree with others, and we bring new points about A and D. Provide explicit facts: A unfriendly, eats unhealthily, unorganized, not good at taking criticism; D moody, loner, arrogant, weak leadership. Then conclude vote remains Candidate C.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
